\t\t\t\t\t\t>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tFact Sheets\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<li class=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tclass=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-link is-current\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\thref=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/releases/\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\taria-label=\"Releases\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tReleases\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<li class=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tclass=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-link\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\thref=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/remarks/\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\taria-label=\"Remarks\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tRemarks\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<li class=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tclass=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-link\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\thref=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/research/\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\taria-label=\"Research\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tResearch\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</ul>\n\t\t</div>\n\t</nav>\n\t</div>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<p>Today, President Donald J. Trump returns to Texas with a record to match the visit: tax relief in workers’ pockets, the most secure border in a generation, safer streets, and a surge of private investment creating new American jobs across the state.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-historic-tax-relief-for-texas-workers-families-seniors\"><strong>Historic Tax Relief for Texas Workers, Families, Seniors</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>President Trump’s Working Families Tax Cuts put money back in Texans’ pockets.</strong></p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>No Tax on Overtime:</strong> Approximately <a href=\"https://dallasexpress.com/state/everything-bigger-in-texas-average-4344-tax-refund-boosted-by-trumps-historic-tax-relief/\">one in four</a> Texas workers no longer pay federal income taxes on qualifying overtime pay.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>No Tax on Social Security:</strong> About four million Texas seniors <a href=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Texas-WH-OBBB-Savings-by-State.pdf\">benefit</a> from the new senior deduction.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Bigger Refunds:</strong> Texas taxpayers saw average refunds of <a href=\"https://upgradedpoints.com/news/average-tax-refunds-by-state-county/\">$4,344</a> — the second-highest in the nation.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Rural Health Investments:</strong> Texas <a href=\"https://scdailygazette.com/2025/12/30/sc-to-receive-200m-in-first-rural-hospital-funding-allocation/\">secured</a> about $281 million in first-year Rural Health Transformation Program funding.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Protecting Jobs and Wages:</strong> The Working Families Tax Cuts <a href=\"https://nam.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/NAM_Tax_Wins_Collection_Final.pdf#page=45\">safeguarded</a> 547,000 Texas jobs, $107 billion in state GDP, and $51 billion in workers’ wages.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-safer-streets-across-texas\"><strong>Safer Streets Across Texas</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Violent crime is falling across the state as a result of President Trump’s law-and-order agenda.</strong></p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Violent crime <a href=\"https://www.dps.texas.gov/sites/default/files/documents/crimereports/25/2025cit.pdf\">fell</a> 13% last year, including a 13% drop in murder and 11% drop in rape.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>The top 25 most populous jurisdictions in Texas all posted <a href=\"https://www.dps.texas.gov/sites/default/files/documents/crimereports/25/2025cit.pdf#page=8\">lower</a> overall crime rates than the year before.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>In the first half of 2026, Arlington homicides <a href=\"https://counciloncj.org/homicide-likely-reaching-a-new-historic-low-as-most-crime-rates-continue-to-decline-at-mid-year/\">fell</a> 60% from the first half of 2025.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>America’s Safest Big Cities recently <a href=\"https://smartasset.com/data-studies/americas-safest-big-cities-2026-study\">placed</a> Plano, Laredo, and Arlington in the national Top 20 — with Plano and Laredo in the Top 10.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-the-most-secure-border-in-a-generation\"><strong>The Most Secure Border in a Generation</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>President Trump ended the Biden-era border crisis and is reimbursing Texas for the costs it carried.</strong></p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>The Trump Administration <a href=\"https://www.dhs.gov/news/2026/08/13/trump-administration-delivers-15-straight-months-zero-releases-border\">has not released</a> a single illegal alien at the border for 15 straight months through July.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Southern border apprehensions in July were <a href=\"https://www.dhs.gov/news/2026/08/13/trump-administration-delivers-15-straight-months-zero-releases-border\">94% lower</a> than the monthly average under Biden.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Refugee admissions in the first ten months of this fiscal year are <a href=\"https://www.pewresearch.org/short-reads/2026/08/17/refugee-admissions-to-the-us-are-dropping-sharply-in-trumps-second-term/#:~:text=The%20federal%20government%20has%20admitted%2010%2C258%20refugees%20through%20the%20first%2010%20months%20of%20fiscal%20year%202026%2C%20which%20ends%20on%20Sept.%2030.%20That%E2%80%99s%20down%20from%2038%2C102%20refugees%20in%20fiscal%202025%20and%20100%2C034%20in%20fiscal%202024.%20(President%20Joe%20Biden%20was%20in%20office%20for%20part%20of%20fiscal%202025%20and%20all%20of%20fiscal%202024.)\">down almost 90%</a> from 2024.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>The Working Families Tax Cuts <a href=\"The%20Working%20Families%20Tax%20Cuts%20invest%20$46.5%20billion%20to%20complete%20hundreds%20of%20miles%20of%20the%20border%20wall%20and%20deploy%20advanced%20surveillance%20technology%20alongside%20it.\">allocated</a> $46.5 billion to finish the border wall.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Texas is set to <a href=\"https://www.texastribune.org/2026/08/24/texas-border-reimbursement-cornyn-abbott-operation-lone-star/\">receive</a> $7.5 billion from the State Border Security Reinforcement Fund — established in the Working Families Tax Cuts — to recoup costs from the Biden-era border crisis.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-protecting-texas-communities\"><strong>Protecting Texas Communities</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>President Trump is delivering for Texas farmers, ranchers, and everyday families.</strong></p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Water for the Valley: </strong><a>In January 2026, USDA and the State Department </a><a href=\"https://www.usda.gov/about-usda/news/press-releases/2026/02/03/statement-secretary-state-marco-rubio-and-secretary-agriculture-brooke-rollins\">secured</a> Mexico’s commitment to deliver 350,000 acre-feet per year from the Rio Grande — meeting the 1944 treaty average and repaying prior-cycle debt.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Protecting Ratepayers: </strong>After President Trump’s landmark Ratepayer Protection Pledge, the Public Utility Commission of Texas and ERCOT <a href=\"https://gov.texas.gov/news/post/governor-abbott-announces-puc-and-ercot-actions-protecting-residential-ratepayers-from-data-center-costs\">moved to shield</a> Texas families from the cost of data center expansion.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Screwworm Response: </strong>The Trump Administration <a href=\"https://gov.texas.gov/news/post/governor-abbott-announces-federal-funding-to-strengthen-nws-inspection-capacity\">funded</a> additional Texas Animal Health Commission inspectors and a new <a href=\"https://texasscorecard.com/state/texas-receives-federal-funding-to-combat-screwworm/\">$750 million sterile-fly facility</a>, which <a href=\"https://www.usda.gov/about-usda/news/press-releases/2026/04/17/usda-and-us-army-corps-engineers-break-ground-new-texas-sterile-fly-production-facility\">broke ground</a> in April at Moore Air Base in Edinburg.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-a-private-investment-boom-in-texas\"><strong>A Private Investment Boom in Texas</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>President Trump’s agenda of tax cuts, energy dominance, secure borders, and pro-growth policies has drawn major capital to the Lone Star State.</strong></p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Bristol Myers Squibb <a href=\"https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20260810766100/en/Bristol-Myers-Squibb-Advances-U.S.-Manufacturing-Investment-with-New-%242.3-Billion-Campus-in-Houston-Texas?utm_campaign=shareaholic&amp;utm_medium=twitter&amp;utm_source=socialnetwork\">announced</a> a $2.3 billion investment to build a new multi-modal manufacturing campus in Houston.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Toyo Co. <a href=\"https://www.plantservices.com/industry-news/news/55398083/toyo-co-invests-357-million-to-build-hjt-solar-cell-manufacturing-facility-in-texas\">announced</a> a $357 million investment to build a solar cell manufacturing facility near Houston, creating 400 American jobs.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Toyota <a href=\"https://www.axios.com/2026/07/06/toyota-pickups-texas-mexico\">announced</a> a $3.6 billion investment at its San Antonio campus to build the new Tacoma in the United States instead of Mexico, creating 2,000 American jobs.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Saronic <a href=\"https://news.usni.org/2026/07/16/saronic-announces-texas-site-for-new-3-2b-shipyard\">announced</a> it will build a new $3.2 billion shipyard in Brownsville.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Micron <a href=\"https://investors.micron.com/news/press-release/2026/Micron-Announces-Up-to-3-Billion-Strategic-Investment-to-Strengthen-U-S--Semiconductor-Ecosystem/default.aspx#:~:text=As%20part%20of,the%20United%20States.\">announced</a> $500 million in strategic financing to advance development and manufacturing at its Sherman facility.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>FormFactor <a href=\"https://gov.texas.gov/news/post/governor-abbott-announces-texas-semiconductor-innovation-fund-grant-to-formfactor#:~:text=The%20advanced%20manufacturing%20facility%20is,choosing%20Texas%20for%20this%20expansion.\">announced</a> a $140 million investment for a new probe card manufacturing facility in Farmers Branch, creating more than 600 American jobs.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>In July, ZERLUMA <a href=\"https://www.rgvbusinessjournal.com/news/28/07/2026/mission-zerluma-50-million-aluminum-manufacturing-plant/\">broke ground</a> on a $50 million aluminum recycling and advanced manufacturing facility in Mission.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>SpaceX <a href=\"https://gov.texas.gov/news/post/governor-abbott-announces-spacex-expansion-in-grimes-county\">announced</a> a $16.8 billion investment for the first phase of its new semiconductor fabrication plant in Grimes County.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>USG Corporation <a href=\"https://gov.texas.gov/news/post/governor-abbott-announces-usg-corporation-expansion-in-orange\">announced</a> a $1.18 billion investment to build a new production facility in Orange, creating 200 American jobs.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Grupo Bimbo <a href=\"https://commercialbaking.com/grupo-bimbo-commits-1-billion-to-elevate-us-business/\">announced</a> a $1 billion investment affirming its commitment to the U.S. market.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>XPEL <a href=\"https://www.tradingview.com/news/tradingview:ce3a10126fe4b:0-xpel-acquires-60-4m-san-antonio-site-adds-44-8m-pnc-loan-and-amends-wells-fargo-facility/\">announced</a> a $60 million investment to expand manufacturing and operations in San Antonio.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Tesla <a href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/sectors/technology/articles/tesla-plans-3-billion-texas-182124922.html?guccounter=1\">announced</a> a $3 billion investment in a research chip facility at its Giga Texas campus.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Avant Technology <a href=\"https://gov.texas.gov/news/post/governor-abbott-announces-texas-semiconductor-innovation-fund-grant-to-avant-technology\">announced</a> a $20 million investment to expand its manufacturing facility in Pharr, creating 250 American jobs.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>America First Refining and Reliance <a href=\"https://www.foxbusiness.com/energy/trump-touts-historic-300b-texas-refinery-first-new-us-plant-nearly-50-years\">announced</a> a multi-billion-dollar energy partnership to open the first new U.S. oil refinery in nearly half a century in Brownsville.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>MP Materials <a href=\"https://www.wsj.com/business/rare-earth-miner-mp-materials-to-invest-more-than-1-25-billion-in-new-texas-factory-2b6e745a?gaa_at=eafs&amp;gaa_n=AWEtsqcUpFpJsCe-CqF_h5P41jC2W69xtLZnzljz9J1GUXB5r0H7CAgUGfbk&amp;gaa_ts=69a1fc36&amp;gaa_sig=QEqvmvCcJUIUbDNQ_Lliw8idMTWdffytVMRbyQ6vi7KwHCjusvtVNcusfGtQiLsBQHICUZWnfHx56B-tYcTNFw%3D%3D\">announced</a> a more than $1.25 billion investment in a new large-scale rare-earth magnet manufacturing campus in Northlake, creating more than 1,500 direct manufacturing and engineering jobs.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Arm Inc. <a href=\"https://gov.texas.gov/news/post/governor-abbott-announces-texas-semiconductor-innovation-fund-grant-to-arm-inc\">announced</a> a $71 million investment to expand its Austin campus with a new semiconductor lab, creating more than 320 American jobs.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Vantage Data Centers <a href=\"https://www.reuters.com/business/vantage-data-centers-plans-25-billion-ai-campus-texas-2025-08-19/\">announced</a> a $25 billion investment to build a 1,200-acre data center campus in Shackelford County.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Inventec <a href=\"https://www.taipeitimes.com/News/biz/archives/2025/06/17/2003838724\">announced</a> an $85 million investment to build a manufacturing base in Texas to support AI server shipments.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Wistron <a href=\"https://www.reuters.com/technology/wistron-corp-invest-additional-455-million-new-us-unit-2025-05-06/\">announced</a> a $500 million investment to acquire land and facilities in Dallas for high-performance computing devices.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>LGM Pharma <a href=\"https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20250312785272/en/LGM-Pharma-Invests-%246M-in-U.S.-Drug-Manufacturing-Capabilities-for-Liquids-Suspensions-Semi-Solids-and-Suppositories\">announced</a> a $6 million investment to expand its Rosenberg manufacturing facility.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Paris Baguette <a href=\"https://www.manufacturingdive.com/news/paris-baguette-plans-first-us-bakery-plant-Texas-160-million-investment/740929/\">announced</a> a $160 million investment to build the company’s first North American production site, creating 450 American jobs.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\" />\n\n\n\n<p><strong>President Trump and Republicans are proving once again that America First means Texas First</strong> — lower taxes, a sealed border, safer communities, and jobs that stay in the United States.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/releases/2026/08/president-trump-delivers-for-texas-lower-taxes-border-security-and-jobs-coming-home/\">President Trump Delivers for Texas: Lower Taxes, Border Security, and Jobs Coming Home</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov\">The White House</a>.</p>",
